@tradition first-fruits
// First-fruit supper: Greening, week 7, Monday dinner (day 134 in the first year). The seedlings from Greening's
// Sowing morning (day 97) give their first crop, and a bowl of it goes on every table in the mess at dinner. Lighter
// than the plan's full supper: an ordinary dinner with the first fruits on the tables, so the galley's day is the same.
// A meal tradition: those going eat dinner here (ties galley meal=dinner). Monday, so it never meets the weekend's
// traditions; it ends before running club (19:15, the gym). Design note: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md.
k: 475
title: First-fruit supper
when: quarter week 7 monday season greening
at: 18:15-19:05
min: 25
prio: 1
jitter: 10
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: cruz-tove always, garden always, gardener 90%, garden-lover 80%, galley 60%, everyone 45%
anim: talk
host: cruz-tove
from: cruz-tove
ties: galley meal=dinner dish=first-fruits
ties: garden harvest
invite: host=oneill-imani odds=30% line="The first fruits are in. There's a bowl on every table at dinner. Come and try one?"

== mail
- The new beds have their first crop. First-fruit supper tomorrow at dinner, {time}: a bowl on every table in the mess. One each, please. The garden counted.

== ask
- First fruits at dinner tonight. I've been watching those plants for weeks.
- Dinner in the mess tonight. The first strawberries are out.
- Don't be late to dinner. The first fruits go fast.   #funny

== here
- Try one. Go on. We grew those.   #warm
- Sweeter than last year. Don't tell the old beds.   #funny
- Six weeks from seed to this. Not bad for a ship.

== thanks
- You take one of the first fruits from the bowl. It tastes of summer, somewhere far away.   #warm

== chatter
- Did you get a first fruit? I got two. Nobody saw.   #funny
- The first crop of {season} is always the best. Ask anyone in the garden.
- Tove checks every plant twice before the first-fruit supper.
